NAME

ulibParseFidoNetAddress - Converts a string into a FidoNet address


SYNOPSIS

void ulibParseFidoNetAddress(UBYTE *String, struct FidoNetAddress *Fido)
                                    a0                    a1


DESCRIPTION

This function converts a string from one of the formats shown below, into a
(struct FidoNetAddress):

   Type                   Example
   -------------------    -----------
   Zone:Net/Node.Point    1:250/642.0
   Zone:Net/Node          1:250/642
   Net/Node               250/642
   Zone:Net/Node.*        1:250/642.*
   Zone:Net/*             1:250/*
   Zone:*                 1:*
   *                      *

The point part of the string is optional (it is assumed to be zero if no
point is given).

The zone part of the string is mandatory unless the (struct FidoNetAddress)
is filled out with a non-zero zone prior to calling this function, in which
case the provided zone will be used as the default.

This function also recognises the * wildcard (see above examples).  For
addresses of the form Zone:Net/Node.*, the Point element will be set equal
to FIDOADDR_MATCH_ALL, which happens to equal negative one (-1).

Similarly, for addresses of the form Zone:Net/*, the Node element will be set
to FIDOADDR_MATCH_ALL, for addresses of the form Zone:*, the Net element will
be set to FIDOADDR_MATCH_ALL, and for address of the form *, the Zone element
will be set to FIDOADDR_MATCH_ALL.

If any wildcards are used, this function will return a non-zero return code
(see below).

Note that you should clear the (struct FidoNetAddress) before using it,
since (struct FidoNetAddress) contains space for Domain addressing, which
will be supported in Xenolink 2.0.


RETURNS

0        - Success
1        - Failure, no zone present
2        - Failure, missing slash ( / )
3        - Failure, missing colon ( : )
10       - Success, address is of format *
11       - Success, address is of format Zone:*
12       - Success, address is of format Zone:Net/*
13       - Success, address is of format Zone:Net/Node.*
